### Stack / buffer honesty
| Layer | What happens | Class |
|-------|----------------|-------|
| Ident accumulate | `str_slice` once per span | **path-A** — no O(token²) concat |
| Runtime `oo_str_slice` (`chs_rt_str.c:197`) | one `oo_str_alloc_payload` + `memcpy` of the span | O(\|ident\|) heap, honest |
| Walk `char_at` | runtime 1-char `OoStr` per visit (`oo_char_at`) | O(\|args\|) 1-byte temps — **language floor**, not 7.1 concat leak |
| C stack `char buf[N]` | not expressible in `.oo` | not required for alpha close |

Complexity: time O(|args|) char visits; aux = O(1) scalars + one token
slice at a time. No growing concat buffer.

